Subject: Rebase gpgscm's string port cursor from the new buffer
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

realloc_port_string moved the write cursor with curr -= start - str. That
yields the right address, but under Fil-C the pointer keeps the capability
of the old buffer, which is freed just after, so the next character
written to a grown string port (gpgscm's t-child test) trapped as a use
after free. Add the cursor's offset to the new buffer instead.

diff --git a/tests/gpgscm/scheme.c b/tests/gpgscm/scheme.c
index bde39fc..88ccb74 100644
--- a/tests/gpgscm/scheme.c
+++ b/tests/gpgscm/scheme.c
@@ -2078,7 +2078,7 @@ static int realloc_port_string(scheme *sc, port *p)
     memcpy(str, start, old_size);
     p->rep.string.start=str;
     p->rep.string.past_the_end=str+new_size-1;
-    p->rep.string.curr-=start-str;
+    p->rep.string.curr=str+(p->rep.string.curr-start);
     sc->free(start);
     return 1;
   } else {
